le.txt\\\", you can type \\\"touch file.txt\\\" and press enter. This will create a new empty file called \\\"file.txt\\\".\\n9. \\\"cat\\\": This command is used to concatenate or join multiple files into one. For example, if you want to join two files called \\\"file1.txt\\\" and \\\"file2.txt\\\" into a new file called \\\"file3.txt\\\", you can type \\\"cat file1.txt file2.txt > file3.txt\\\" and press enter. This will join the contents of \\\"file1.txt\\\" and \\\"file2.txt\\\" into a new file called \\\"file3.txt\\\".\\n10. \\\"clear\\\": This command is used to clear the terminal screen. For example, if you want to clear the terminal screen, you can type \\\"clear\\\" and press enter. This will clear the terminal screen and show you a clean slate.\\n\\nThese are just a few examples of the many Linux commands available. It's important to note that these commands can be used in different ways and combined with other commands to perform more complex tasks.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/457", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"write me an invoice form for a moving business\", \"response\": \"Here is a sample invoice form for a moving business:\\n\\nMoving Invoice Form:\\n\\nCustomer Information:\\n\\nName: \\nAddress: \\nCity: \\nState: \\nZip Code: \\nPhone Number: \\nEmail Address: \\nMoving Date: \\nMoving From: \\nMoving To: \\nNumber of Movers: \\nNumber of Hours: \\nTotal Cost: \\nPayment Method: \\nCash\\nCheck\\nCredit Card\\nOther: \\nSignature: \\n\\nNotes:\\n\\nPlease provide a detailed list of items being moved, including any special handling or packing requirements.\\nAll payments are due at the time of the move.\\nWe reserve the right to refuse service to anyone.\\nBy signing below, you acknowledge that you have read and understand the terms and conditions of our moving services.\\n\\nSignature of Customer: \\nSignature of Witness: \\nDate:\\n\\nNote: It is recommended to include any additional information or policies specific to your moving business, such as cancellation fees or damage liability.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": 