{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/991", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I will ask you question of subject Management Information System this subject is of computer application give answers to the questions in very simple, easy to understand and in context of Management Information System subject\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nOK, no problem! What is your question?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nDiscuss Service Process Cycle and Analysis\", \"response\": \"The Service Process Cycle and Analysis is a framework for understanding and improving the service delivery process within an organization. It consists of five main stages:\\n \\n\\n 1. Service Request: This is the first stage of the service delivery process, where a customer or user submits a request for a service.\\n \\n\\n 2. Service Design: In this stage, the service is designed and documented, including the service level agreement (SLA) and the processes and procedures to be followed.\\n \\n\\n 3. Service Transition: This stage involves the deployment and implementation of the service, including testing, training, and change management.\\n \\n\\n 4. Service Operation: This is the stage where the service is actively delivered to the customer or user, and any incidents or problems that arise are resolved.\\n \\n\\n 5. Service Improvement: This is the final stage of the service delivery process, where the service is evaluated and improved based on customer feedback and other metrics.\\n \\n\\n By going through each of these stages, an organization can ensure that its service delivery process is efficient, effective, and meets the needs of its customers. Additionally, analysis tools such as process mapping, flow charts, and service level reporting can be used to identify areas for improvement and ensure that the service delivery process is constantly evolving and improving.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/446", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I am asking an AI to how to present the example and solution which I had given like this:\\n\\\"Take the example and compare it to the solution, how the solution is coming from the example to get the solution\\nLike in this way:\\nFrom the EXAMPLE [A] words this leads to the solution in the SOLUTION [A] and also give,why it's this[A] in EXAMPLE leads to this[A] in solution, also interlink in between them for comparison,why this  [A] in EXAMPLE is not the [B] in solution & Vice-versa,also describe innner meaning of this [A] in EXAMPLE to the SOLUTION\\\" \\nCan you correct the what I am asking in highlighted area with a better & also give some other examples of prompts to which I can ask for an AI\", \"response\": \"Here is a corrected version of the prompt: \\n\\n\\\"Take the example and compare it to the solution, showing how the solution is derived from the example. Explain how specific aspects of the example lead to specific aspects of the solution, and describe the inner meaning of these aspects. Highlight the similarities and differences between the example and the solution, and explain why certain aspects of the example are not present in the solution, and vice versa. Use concrete examples and language to make the comparison clear and easy to understand.\\\"\\n\\nSome other examples of prompts that could be used to generate similar content include:\\n\\n\\\"Analyze the similarities and differences between two different approaches to solving a problem, and explain how each approach leads to a different solution.\\\"\\n\\\"Compare and contrast two different theories or concepts, and explain how each theory or concept leads to different conclusions or outcomes.\\\"\\n\\\"Examine the relationship between a specific phenomenon and its underlying causes, and explain how understanding this relationship can lead to solutions or interventions.\\\"\\n\\\"Explore the ways in which a specific event or experience has influenced the development of a particular field or area of study, and explain how this influence has led to new insights or innovations.\\\"\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/822", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"When I turn my computer on, all I see is a black screen with this: \\n\\\"DISK BOOT FAILURE - INSERT SYSTEM DISK AND PRESS ENTER\\\"\\n\\\"No boot device available, press Enter to continue\\\"\\nWhat should I do?\", \"response\": \"# Ways to fix the Disk Boot Failure Error\\n\\nThe disk boot failure error occurs when the system fails to load your operating system correctly. This happens if the BIOS fails to detect a disk that has the operating system on it. Therefore, the BIOS throws an error message, *\\\"Disk boot failure - insert system disk and press enter.\\\"* It means that the BIOS is requesting the user to add or insert a disk drive that has the operating system installed.\\n\\nHere are some steps you can try to resolve this issue:\\n\\n1.  **Check the boot order in the BIOS:** Make sure that the computer is set to boot from the hard drive that contains the operating system.\\n\\n2.  **Check the hard drive:** Make sure that the hard drive is properly connected and has not failed. You can try connecting the hard drive to another computer to see if it can be detected.\\n\\n3.  **Check the bootable media:** If you are trying to boot from a bootable USB drive or CD, make sure that it is properly inserted and that the computer is set to boot from that device.\\n\\n4.  **Check the boot sector:** If the boot sector of the hard drive is corrupted, it may prevent the computer from booting. You can try running a boot sector repair utility, like *chkdsk* on Windows, to fix the issue.\\n\\n5.  **Remove newly installed hardware:** The disk boot failure error can occur if you installed new internal or external hardware to your computer and did not configure it properly. Trying removing the new hardware and see if this resolves the error.\\n\\n6.  **Restore the computer to a previous state:** If you have a system restore point or a backup, you can try restoring the computer to a previous state when it was working correctly.\\n\\n***If none of these steps resolve the issue, it is recommended that you get the help of a computer technician.***\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
