{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/470", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"X.org 6.8.1 mouse cursor on Fooware MV1005 vid. chipset - is misshapen\", \"response\": \"If you are experiencing a misshapen mouse cursor in X.org version 6.8.1 with a Fooware MV1005 video chipset, it is likely due to a compatibility issue between the X.org server and the video chipset. This issue can be caused by a lack of support for the particular video chipset in the X.org server, or by a bug in the server's handling of the chipset.\\n\\nTo resolve this issue, you can try updating the X.org server to a newer version, if available, or try using a different window manager or desktop environment that may have better compatibility with your video chipset. You can also try using a different mouse cursor theme to see if that resolves the issue.\\n\\nAdditionally, you can try installing the proprietary drivers provided by Fooware for the MV1005 chipset, if available, as these drivers may provide better support for the chipset and resolve the issue with the misshapen mouse cursor.\\n\\nIf you are unable to resolve the issue with these steps, you may need to contact the developers of X.org or Fooware for further assistance.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "sof